From 76155f39cf669146fcb38445391af0d114e979e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:17:54 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Interface: a port's own look and sounds for the game's
 dialogs

ui::set_dialog_skin(DialogSkin) lets a port draw the dialogs the game asks
the PSP for, the message dialog, the save-data list and the game's keyboard,
in its own look. PortableKit keeps what they do: the answers, the saves, the
typing and the controls. The skin gets a view of what the dialog shows each
frame and says what the pointer is over and what it clicked. A dialog without
a skin, or whose skin is not available that frame, is drawn as before.

DialogSkin::sound hears what a skinned dialog did (the selection moved,
something was chosen, the player backed out, a key was refused), for a port
that plays the game's own sounds.

When skinned, the save list moves with up and down (arrow keys, D-pad, left
stick, mouse wheel) and stays drawn behind its question. SaveSlot carries the
save's ICON0.PNG, and disc_image_path() says which disc image is open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
